# Project Rules for AI Agents

## Code Style

- Use TypeScript strictly; avoid `any` unless necessary
- Prefer small, focused modules over large “god” files
- Use meaningful names; keep functions small and focused
- Rust collector: keep the hook path minimal, no network, no text logging

## Naming

- Prefer **kebab-case** for file names (e.g. `collector-runner.ts`, `live-server.ts`)
- Keep exported symbols idiomatic (e.g. `runCollectSession` is fine), but keep **file paths** kebab-case
- Avoid oversimplified names for locals and callback params (e.g. `v`, `d`, `c`, `e`); prefer descriptive names like `event`, `stats`, `scanCode`, `sessionStartedAt`

## Commit Messages

Use [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/):

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>
```

- **feat:** new feature (MINOR)
- **fix:** bug fix (PATCH)
- **docs:** documentation only
- **style:** formatting, no code change
- **refactor:** code change that neither fixes nor adds a feature
- **perf:** performance improvement
- **test:** adding or updating tests
- **chore:** build, CI, tooling
- **BREAKING CHANGE:** use `!` after type/scope or footer (MAJOR)

Example: `feat(live-server): add reset stats endpoint`

## Versioning & Changelog

- Use [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/): MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
- Version lives in `package.json` and `collector/Cargo.toml` (keep them in sync)
- When releasing: bump both versions, update `CHANGELOG.md` (move `[Unreleased]` into a dated `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`), update `README.md` version line
- Changelog entries must describe **actual user-facing changes** included in the release (derived from commits/diff since the previous release), not just “bump version”

### Changelog format

- Follow [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/)
- File: `CHANGELOG.md` at project root
- Sections: `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Deprecated`, `### Removed`, `### Fixed`, `### Security`
- Unreleased work: `## [Unreleased] — X.Y.Z` (no release date until cut)
- Released entry format: `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`
- Add new entries at the top (above previous releases)
- Do **not** add filler entries like “version bump for release”; if a release contains no notable changes, do not cut a release (or explicitly document why)

### Version bump rules

- **PATCH** — bug fixes, minor tweaks
- **MINOR** — new features, non-breaking changes
- **MAJOR** — breaking changes (use `BREAKING CHANGE` in commit)

## Editing

- Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones
- Preserve existing formatting and indentation
- After substantive edits, sanity-check with `npm run report` (and rebuild collector when Rust changes: `npm run build:collector`)

## Project Context

- Local **Windows** tool: physical keyboard press heatmap for deciding which switches to replace first
- Stack: **Node.js + TypeScript** CLI/orchestrator (`tsx`) + thin **Rust** collector (`WH_KEYBOARD_LL`)
- Privacy-first: offline; no typed text / window titles / layout logging; live HTTP binds **`127.0.0.1` only**
- Counts **physical keys** (scan code + extended flag), not characters — EN/RU layouts share the same key
- Runtime data under `data/` (gitignored): `stats.json`, `heatmap.html`
- Docs: `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`
- No React/Vite/UI framework — heatmap is server-rendered / static HTML from `templates/heatmap.html`
- Follow existing patterns; check README before adding dependencies

## Key Behaviors

- **`npm run build:collector`** — `cargo build --release` into `collector/target/release/collector.exe` (explicit `--target-dir`)
- **`npm run collect`** — loads/creates `data/stats.json`, spawns Rust collector, parses NDJSON key-down events, flushes stats periodically; Ctrl+C stops, finalizes recording interval, writes static heatmap
- **Live view** — during collect, `http://127.0.0.1:17823/` (~1s partial refresh); **LIVE** badge; **Reset stats** (`POST /reset`); **Copy top list**; **Total recorded** / **Saved intervals** / **Recording intervals** (completed start→stop only)
- **Console session timer** — terminal line `session mm:ss · presses N` for the current run only (not shown in the browser); resets with Reset stats
- **`npm run report`** — regenerates static `data/heatmap.html` from saved stats (no Reset button; Copy top list still works)
- **`npm run reset`** — deletes `data/stats.json` and `data/heatmap.html`
- **Key aggregation** — `canonicalKey` / aliases in `keymap.ts` (e.g. RShift `54:0`→`54:1`); collector may normalize RShift/Win/Menu via VK
- **Ignore** key-up and OS auto-repeat (one count per physical press)
- **Heatmap labels** — US QWERTY **positions** for display; not the user’s active layout
- After code pulls, **restart `collect`** so live UI picks up changes (old process keeps old in-memory renderers)

## Component Structure

This is not a React app. Organize as small TypeScript modules + one HTML template + one Rust binary:

- **CLI** — `cli.ts` dispatches `collect` | `report` | `reset`
- **Session runner** — `collector-runner.ts` owns spawn, flush, timers, live server wiring, finalize session
- **Persistence** — `store.ts` (`StatsFile`, load/save/normalize, recording intervals, `formatDuration`)
- **Key map** — `keymap.ts` (scan/ext → label + grid cell; aliases)
- **Report/UI HTML** — `report.ts` renders into `templates/heatmap.html` placeholders (`__BODY__`, `__LIVE_HEAD__`, `__PAGE_SCRIPT__`)
- **Live HTTP** — `live-server.ts` (loopback only; `/`, `/partial`, `/reset`)
- **CLI colors** — `style.ts` (respect `NO_COLOR` / TTY)
- **Rust** — `collector/src/main.rs` emits NDJSON `{ sc, ext, t }` on first key-down only

## Project Structure

```
.
├── package.json          # scripts: build:collector, collect, report, reset
├── tsconfig.json
├── README.md
├── CHANGELOG.md
├── src/
│   ├── cli.ts                 # CLI entry
│   ├── collector-runner.ts    # collect session orchestration
│   ├── live-server.ts         # localhost live heatmap + reset
│   ├── store.ts               # stats.json IO + recording timers
│   ├── keymap.ts              # physical key map + aliases
│   ├── report.ts              # HTML heatmap generation
│   └── style.ts               # terminal colors
├── templates/
│   └── heatmap.html           # static/live HTML shell + CSS
├── collector/
│   ├── Cargo.toml
│   ├── Cargo.lock
│   └── src/main.rs            # WH_KEYBOARD_LL → NDJSON stdout
└── data/                      # gitignored runtime output
    ├── stats.json
    └── heatmap.html
```

Prefer extending these modules over adding new top-level packages or frameworks.

## Communication

- Be direct and concise
- Prefer answering questions before making edits when unclear
- Explain non-obvious changes briefly
